{
  "summary": "Updates `-acceptnonstdtxn=1` (available only on test networks) to skip standard non-mandatory script verification flags during mempool acceptance, checking only consensus script flags instead. It also replaces a heuristic flag-mask check in `CheckInputScripts` with an explicit enum parameter separating block validation from mempool validation, and introduces compile-time assertions to ensure standard verify flags subsume consensus flags.",
  "problem": "On test networks, configuring a node with `-acceptnonstdtxn=1` admits transactions with non-standard formats or output scripts into the mempool, but policy script verification still unconditionally enforced `STANDARD_SCRIPT_VERIFY_FLAGS`. As a result, transactions testing soft-fork upgrades or non-mandatory script rules (such as `OP_SUCCESS`, `OP_NOPx`, or uncompressed keys in SegWit) were rejected from testnet mempools.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: \"This PR changes `-acceptnonstdtxn=1` so that it also skips the non-mandatory script checks, allowing txs that (eg) use OP_NOPx or OP_SUCCESS into the mempool. This remains only available on test nets.\""
